$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Amination: Diethyl
1-amino-3-methylpyrrole-2,4-dicarboxylate. A solution of potassium
t-butoxide (1 M, 110 mL) was added to asolution of pyrrole (22.5 g, 10.0
mol) in NMP (130 mL) at 20 °C. After 20 min, a solution of aminating
reagent (11.5 mol) in NMP (80 mL) was added at greater than 25 °C. The
mixture was stirred at 20 °C for 20 min. The conversion of BMS-529303 was
determined by HPLC analysis. The reaction mixture was treated with brine
(7%, 400 mL) and ethyl acetate (400 mL). The organic layer was separated
and the aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl acetate (400 mL). The
combined organic layers were washed with aqueous sodium bicarbonate
solution (5%, 300 mL) and then water (300 mL). The organic solution was
dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate and concentrated to give a crude
(23.7 g). The crude copmpound was purified by flash chromatography on
silica gel (elute with 5-15% of ethylacetate in heptane). Ethyl
1-amino-2-(n-propylcarboxamido)-3-methylpyrrole-4-carboxylate , yield
86%. mp 97-99 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
