$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of 3 -7 To
an nitrogen-filled flask equipped with a stirring bar, [Cp*RhCl2]2 (15.5
mg, 2.5 mmol %) and CsOAc (191 mg, 1.0 mmol, 2.0 equiv) were added.
Substrate 1 (0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv), PivOH (24 mg, 0.25 mmol, 0.5 equiv)
and dry MeOH (2.5 mL) were added under a stream of nitrogen. Benzoate 2
or 6 (0.75 mmol, 1.5 equiv) was added to the solution and the reaction
was allowed to stir at 50 °C for a period as indicated. After cooling to
room temperature, H2O (3 mL) and EtOAc (5 mL) were added. The organic
layer was collected and the aqueous layer was washed with EtOAc (5 mL x
2). The combined organic fraction was dried over Na2SO4 and then
filtered. After removal of the solvent, the resulting residue was
purified on silica gel column chromatograghy to give product 3 or 7.
5-Methyl-2-(2-morpholinophenyl)-1H-pyrazol-3(2H)-one (3aa)
Methyl-5-oxo-1-(2-((tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)amino)phenyl)-2,5-dihydro-1H-pyrazole-3-carbox
ylate (7i). White solid, 86% yield. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO) δ 7.23 (t, J =
7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.14 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 6.89 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 6.68 (t,
J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.95 (s, 1H), 3.76 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 5H), 3.51 (s, 1H),
3.39 (t, J = 10.3 Hz, 2H), 1.83 (d, J = 11.8 Hz, 2H), 1.27 (dt, J = 14.0,
6.9 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, DMSO) δ 162.7, 154.2, 142.6, 130.1, 127.8,
123.7, 116.3, 113.3, 88.9, 65.9, 52.0, 48.4, 33.0; EI-MS (m/z) 317 (M+),
HRMS calcd for C16H19N3O4 [M+] 317.1376, found 317.1383.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rh(III)-Catalyzed Intermolecular C-H Amination of
1-Aryl-1H-pyrazol-5(4H)-ones with Alkylamines
