$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure D: Synthesis of indolines
via Pd-catalyzed intramolecular amination of δ -C(sp2)-H bonds (condition
B). A mixture of picolinamide (1.0 mmol, 1.0 eq), Pd(OAc)2 (1.1 mg, 0.005
mmol, 0.005 eq), PhI(OAc)2 (645 mg, 2.0 mmol, 2.0 eq) and toluene (8 mL)
in a 20 mL glass vial (purged with Ar, sealed with PTFE cap) was heated
at 80 °C for 24 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt, and
concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was purified by silica gel
flash chromatography to give the cyclized product. Compound 10 was
prepared following the standard procedure D in 86% yield. 1H NMR (CDCl3,
300 MHz) δ 9.11 (s, 1H), 8.64 (td, J = 1.2, 4.8 Hz, 1H), 7.92-7.85 (m,
3H), 7.43 (m, 1H), 7.34 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 4.56 (t, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H),
3.27 (t, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ 166.78, 153.78,
148.50, 148.08, 144.82, 140.23, 137.68, 126.00, 125.11, 124.86, 120.12,
113.00, 51.47, 29.05; HRMS Calcd for C14H12N3O3 [M+H+]: 270.0873; Found:
270.0860.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, capped vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Improved Protocol for Indoline Synthesis via Palladium-Catalyzed
Intramolecular C(sp2)-H Amination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM He, Gang; Lu, Chengxi; Zhao, Yingsheng; Nack, William A.; Chen, Gong
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(12), 2944-2947

