$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure. A mixture of
N-aryl-2-aminopyridine 1 (0.5 mmol), Cu(OAc)2 (20 mol% or 100 mol%),
Fe(NO3)3·9H2O (10 mol%), PivOH (2.5 mmol) in DMF (1.0 mL) was stirred at
130 °C under balloon pressure of O2. The reaction was cooled down to room
temperature after complete consumption of starting material as monitored
by TLC. Water (10 mL), triethylamine (1.0 mL), and EtOAc (10 mL) were
added to the reaction mixture successively. The organic phase was
separated, and the aqueous phase was further extracted with EtOAc (3 × 10
mL). The combined organic layers were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and
concentrated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography to provide
the desired product 2. 4-methylpyrido[1,2-a]benzimidazole (2o). (Time =
23 h), yield: 85%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, D6-DMSO) δ 8.87 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H),
8.23 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H ), 7.83 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.47 (t, J = 7.6 Hz,
1H), 7.35-7.29 (m, 2H) 6.86 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 2.55 (s, 3H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, D6-DMSO) δ 148.8, 144.2, 129.6, 128.3, 126.9, 125.6, 124.9,
121.0, 119.5, 112.4, 110.6, 17.4; HRMS (ESI): Eact mass calcd for
C12H11N2 [M+H]+, 183.0917; Found 183.0920.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Direct Intramolecular C-H Amination Reaction Cocatalyzed by Copper(II)
and Iron(III) as Part of an Efficient Route for the Synthesis of
Pyrido[1,2-a]benzimidazoles from N-Aryl-2-aminopyridines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
