$DATUM V-2-3 Stoichiometric Reaction with a Cyclometalated Ruthenium Complex 7
(Scheme 5c) To an oven-dried screw capped vial equipped with a spinvane
triangular-shaped Teflon stirbar were added complex 7 (22.0 mg, 0.05
mmol), AgSbF6 (17.2 mg, 0.05 mmol), NaOAc (4.1 mg, 0.05 mmol), benzoyl
azide (2a, 10.9 µL, 0.09 mmol) or phenyl isocyanate (2a’, 9.8 µL, 0.09
mmol) and 1,2- dichloroethane (0.3 mL) under atmospheric conditions. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 18 h.
2-Phenylpyridine (1a, 71.5 µL, 0.5 mmol) and AcOH (5.8 µL, 0.1 mmol) in
1,2- dichloroethane (0.3 mL) were added to the crude mixture and allowed
to stir at room temperature for 18 h. The resulting mixture was filtered
through a pad of celite and then washed with CH2Cl2 (10 mL x 3). The
solvents were removed under reduced pressure and the crude reaction
mixture was purified by silica gel column chromatography with
n-hexane/EtOAc as an eluent. The desired product. Yield: 85%.
N-[2-(Pyridin-2-yl)phenyl]benzamide (4a) m.p. 113-114 °C; 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 13.33 (s, 1H), 8.80 (dd, J = 8.3, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 8.64 (d, J =
4.9 Hz, 1H), 8.03 (dd, J = 7.9, 1.7 Hz, 2H), 7.85 - 7.72 (m, 2H), 7.70
(dd, J = 7.9, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.56 - 7.40 (m, 4H), 7.25 (ddd, J = 7.1, 4.9,
1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.18 (td, J = 7.6, 1.3 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
165.4, 158.2, 147.2, 138.1, 137.8, 135.7, 131.4, 130.1, 128.7, 128.5,
127.3, 125.4, 123.5, 122.9, 121.9, 121.8; IR (cm-1) 3053, 2923, 1665,
1586, 1472, 1436, 1313, 1242, 752, 694; HRMS (EI+) m/z calcd. for
C18H14N2O [M]+: 274.1106, found: 274.1106.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stoichiometric amount of the catalyst was used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Orthogonal Reactivity of Acyl Azides in C-H Activation: Dichotomy between
C-C and C-N Amidations Based on Catalyst Systems
