$DATUM III-2. Optimization of the Ru-Catalyzed C-N Amidation Reaction (Table 2)
To an oven-dried screw capped vial with a spinvane triangular-shaped
Teflon stirbar were added 2- phenylpyridine (1a, 28.6 µL, 0.2 mmol),
benzoyl azide (2a, 43.7 µL, 0.36 mmol), catalyst, additive, and solvent
(0.5 mL) under atmospheric conditions. The reaction mixture was stirred
in a pre-heated oil bath at the indicated temperature for 18 h. The
reaction was cooled to room temperature, filtered through a pad of celite
and then washed with CH2Cl2 (10 mL x 3). The solvents were removed under
reduced pressure. The crude yield was measured by NMR using
1,1,2,2-tetrachloroethane as an internal standard. Entry: 18 Yield:
(4a)a,b: 85(80) N-[2-(Pyridin-2-yl)phenyl]benzamide (4a) White solid.
m.p. 113-114 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 13.33 (s, 1H), 8.80 (dd, J =
8.3, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 8.64 (d, J = 4.9 Hz, 1H), 8.03 (dd, J = 7.9, 1.7 Hz,
2H), 7.85 - 7.72 (m, 2H), 7.70 (dd, J = 7.9, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.56 - 7.40 (m,
4H), 7.25 (ddd, J = 7.1, 4.9, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.18 (td, J = 7.6, 1.3 Hz,
1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 165.4, 158.2, 147.2, 138.1, 137.8, 135.7,
131.4, 130.1, 128.7, 128.5, 127.3, 125.4, 123.5, 122.9, 121.9, 121.8; IR
(cm-1) 3053, 2923, 1665, 1586, 1472, 1436, 1313, 1242, 752, 694; HRMS
(EI+) m/z calcd. for C18H14N2O [M]+: 274.1106, found: 274.1106.
