$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Unless otherwise noted, all compounds were
synthesized according the general procedure for compound 8. In a 2‐dram
vial equipped with a magnetic stir bar was combined cyclohexylamine (151
μL, 1.32 mmol), iPr2EtN (708 uL, 3.94 mmol) and dichloromethane (3 mL).
The solution was treated with the stock solution of pyridine‐N‐oxide
(1.05 mL, 1.05 mmol, 1M in dichloromethane) followed by PyBroP (651 mg,
1.37 mmol). The reaction was capped and stirred at room temperature
overnight. Upon completion (TLC analysis), the reaction was poured into
saturated sodium bicarbonate (15 mL) and extracted with DCM (3x15 mL).
The organics were washed with brine, dried (Na2SO4) and evacuated. The
crude material was purified by column chromatography (0‐ EtOAc: Heptanes)
to afford the desired product as a white solid (152 mg, 82%) Compound 9
Entry 3 (95 mg, 83%) The methylamine source for this reaction was a 2.0 M
solution in THF (Aldrich). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.08 (d, J=3.2 Hz,
1H), 7.49‐ 7.35 (m, 1H), 6.56 (dd, J=5.0, 7.0 Hz, 1H,) 6.37 (d, J=8.3 Hz,
1H), 4.64 (br. s., 1H), 2.90 (d, J=5.1 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 159.5, 148.1, 137.4, 112.6, 106.1, 29.0. m/z = 109.0 (M+H)+. LCMS =
100% purity.
