$DATUM b. The same quantities of the amine and 2-chloroquinoline, 12 mg (8 mol%)
of Pd(dba)2, 9 mg (9 mol%) of DavePhos, and 36 mg (1.5 equiv) of sodium
tert-butylate were boiled for 7 h. Yield after chromatography (eluent
CH2Cl2–MeOH, 100:1) 57 mg (82%). N-(Adamantan-1-yl)quinolin-6-amine
(XXV), Yield 57 mg (82%), yellow oily substance, exhibits luminescence on
dissolving in organic solvents 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 1.69 br.s (6H,
CH2Ad), 1.97 br.s (6H, CH2Ad), 2.12 br.s (3H, CHAd), 3.72 br.s (1H, NH),
6.95 d (1H, H5Q, 4J 2.5 Hz), 7.10 d.d (1H, H7Q, 3J 9.1, 4J 2.5 Hz), 7.22
d.d (1H, H3Q, 3J 8.2, 4.2 Hz), 7.82 d (1H, H8Q, 3J 9.1 Hz), 7.88 d (1H,
HQ4, 3J 7.8 Hz), 8.59 d.d (1H, H2Q, 3J 4.2, 4J 1.5 Hz). 13C NMR spectrum,
δ, ppm: 29.6 (3C, CHAd), 36.4 (3C, CH2Ad), 42.9 (3C, CH2Ad), 52.2 (1C,
CAd), 108.4 (1C, C7Q), 121.1 (1C, CQ), 124.5 (1C, CQ), 129.6 (1C, CQ4a),
129.8 (1C, CQ), 133.8 (1C, CQ), 143.2 (1C, CQ8a), 144.2 (1C, C6Q), 146.4
(C2Q). Mass spectrum: m/z 279.191 [M + H]+. C19H23N2. Calculated (M + H)
279.186.
