$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure D: A red cap sealed tube
(25-30 ml in volume) equipped with a stirring bar was heated and cooled
under vacuum and back-filled with argon. [Cp*RhCl2]2 (15.5 mg, 0.025
mmol, 5 mol%) and CsOAc (191 mg, 1.0 mmol, 2.0 eq.) were weighed into the
reaction vessel in glovebox. Npivaloyloxybenzamide substrate (1) (0.5
mmol, 1.0 eq.), PivOH (24 mg, 0.25 mmol, 0.5 eq.) and dry MeOH (2.5 mL)
was added under a stream of argon. N-Chloroamine substrate 2 (1.0 mmol,
2.0 eq.) was added to the solution and the reaction was allowed to stir
at room temperature for 16 h. As monitored by TLC analysis, in case of
incomplete conversion, N-Chloroamine and CsOAc (both 1.0 eq. each time)
were added stepwise until TLC analysis indicated maximum conversion. The
reaction mixture was then diluted with EtOAc (2 mL) and filtered through
a short pad of silica. The silica pad was washed with EtOAc (3 x 4 mL).
The combined filtrates were concentrated under reduced pressure using a
rotary evaporator (40-45 °C).
2-(3-Methylpiperidin-1-yl)-N-(pivaloyloxy)benzamide (3bd) as a colorless
oil, yield 260 mg, 0.82 mmol, 82%. RF (pentane/EtOAc 9:1): 0.27; 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 13.90 (s, 1H, NH), 8.16 (dd, J = 7.8, 1.7 Hz, 1H,
CHar), 7.46 (ddd, J = 8.1, 7.2, 1.7 Hz, 1H, CHar), 7.32-7.23 (m, 2H,
CHar), 3.14-3.01 (m, 2H, CH2), 2.73-2.60 (m, 1H, CH), 2.38 (t, J = 10.8,
1H, CH), 1.96-1.74 (m, 4H, CH2), 1.36 (s, 9H, C(CH3)3), 1.11-0.95 (m, 1H,
CH), 0.91 (d, J = 6.4, 3H, CH3). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 176.0 (CO),
164.4 (CO), 152.1 (Cq), 132.8 (CHar), 131.3 (CHar), 126.6 (Cq), 125.9
(CHar), 122.1 (CHar), 61.9 (CH2), 54.8 (CH2), 38.6 (CMe3), 32.3 (CH2),
31.8 (CH), 27.3 (C(CH3)3), 25.9 (CH2), 19.6 (CH3). ESI-MS: calculated
[C18H26N2O3Na]+: 319.2016, found: 319.2017; ATR-FTIR (cm-1): 3682, 2953,
1776, 1691, 1598, 1480, 1454, 1273, 1117, 1090, 1028, 764, 681, 588.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, in case of incomplete conversion, N-chloroamine and CsOAc
(both 1.0 eq. each time) were added stepwise until TLC analysis indicated
maximum conversion, sealed tube used
