$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Unless otherwise noted, all compounds were synthesized according the
general procedure for compound 8. In a 2‐dram vial equipped with a
magnetic stir bar was combined cyclohexylamine (151 μL, 1.32 mmol),
iPr2EtN (708 uL, 3.94 mmol) and dichloromethane (3 mL). The solution was
treated with the stock solution of pyridine‐N‐oxide (1.05 mL, 1.05 mmol,
1M in dichloromethane) followed by PyBroP (651 mg, 1.37 mmol). The
reaction was capped and stirred at room temperature overnight. Upon
completion (TLC analysis), the reaction was poured into saturated sodium
bicarbonate (15 mL) and extracted with DCM (3x15 mL). The organics were
washed with brine, dried (Na2SO4) and evacuated. The crude material was
purified by column chromatography (0‐ EtOAc: Heptanes) to afford the
desired product as a white solid (152 mg, 82%) compound 8, yield 152 mg,
82% 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.10 ‐ 8.02 (m, 1 H), 7.39 (ddd, J=2.0,
7.0, 8.5 Hz, 1H), 6.52 (ddd, J=1.0, 5.0, 7.0 Hz, 1H), 6.36 (d, J=8.5 Hz,
1H), 4.40 (br. d, J=9.0 Hz, 1H), 3.59 ‐ 3.45 (m, 1H), 2.11 - 1.99 (m,
2H), 1.76 (dt, J=3.9, 13.6 Hz, 2H), 1.69 ‐ 1.59 (m, 1H), 1.48 ‐ 1.34 (m,
2H), 1.31 ‐ 1.13 (m, 3 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 149.3; 148.5;
137.5; 112.6; 106.9; 50.4; 33.6; 26.0; 25.1. m/z = 177.2 (M+H)+. LCMS =
100% purity.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
