$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedures for Cu(II)-Mediated C-N
bond formation. To a 15 mL sealed tube was added substrates 1 ( 0.1 mmol,
1 equiv), Cu(OAc)2 (0.1 mmol), TsNH2 (0.2 mmol), Na2CO3 (0.2 mmol), DMSO
(1 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at 80°C for 6 h under air. Upon
completion, EtOAc was added to dilute the mixture and then washed with
NH3·H2O and saturated NaCl(aq). The organic fraction was dried over
Na2SO4, evaporated and purified by flash column chromatography on silica
gel with a gradient eluent of hexane and ethyl acetate or dichloromethane
and methanol.
N-(2-(4,5-dihydrooxazol-2-yl)phenyl)-2-(4-methylphenylsulfonamido)-5-(trifluoromethyl)benzamide
(3q): white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 13.41 (brs, 1H), 11.59 (brs,
1H), 8.79 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 8.28 (s, 1H), 7.90 (dd, J = 7.9, 1.5 Hz,
1H), 7.84-7.75 (m, 3H), 7.63 (dd, J = 8.8, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.57-7.51 (m,
1H), 7.21-7.14 (m, 3H), 4.44 (t, J = 9.5 Hz, 2H), 4.16 (t, J = 9.6 Hz,
2H), 2.30 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.34, 165.03, 144.08,
142.93, 138.98, 136.30, 132.81, 129.73, 129.38, 129.25 (q, J C-F = 3.5
Hz), 127.24, 125.74 (q, J C-F = 3.8 Hz), 124.70 (q, J C-F = 33 Hz),
123.70 (q, J C-F = 271 Hz),123.44, 120.45, 119.79, 119.67, 113.82, 66.57,
54.04, 21.44; HRMS (ESI-TOF) m/z Calcd for C24H20F3N3O4S [M+H]+ 504.1199,
found 504.1203.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, aerobic, sealed tube used
