$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Catalytic Amination Using a Rhodacycle Complex
1a (eq 2) To a screw capped vial equipped with a spinvane
triangular-shaped Teflon stirbar were added 2-phenylpyridine (0.2 mmol),
p-toluenesulfonyl azide (0.22 mmol), complex 1a (4 mol %), AgSbF6 (4 mol
%) and 1,2-dichloroethane (0.5 mL) under atmospheric conditions. The
reaction mixture was stirred in a pre-heated oil bath at 80 °C for 12 h.
The reaction was cooled to room temperature, filtered through a plug of
celite, and then washed with dichloromethane (10 mL x 3). Solvents were
removed under reduced pressure and the crude yield was measured by 1H NMR
using 1,3-benzodioxole as an internal standard.
N-[2-(Pyridin-2-yl)phenyl]-3,5-bis(trifluoromethyl)aniline (5b) White
solid, yield 82%. m.p. 69-71 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.76 (s, 1H),
8.75-8.65 (m, 1H), 7.85 (s, 1H), 7.76 (dd, J = 8.0, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.70
(dd, J = 7.9, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.54-7.48 (m, 1H), 7.39 (d, J = 1.4 Hz, 1H),
7.35-7.26 (m, 3H), 7.12 (d, J = 1.4 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
158.4, 147.6, 144.6, 140.5, 137.4, 133.0, 132.7, 132.3, 132.0, 130.1,
129.9, 127.5, 126.6, 124.8, 122.9, 122.1, 121.8, 121.7, 119.4, 118.0,
116.90, 116.86, 113.2, 113.12, 113.08, 113.05, 113.0; IR (NaCl) ν 1621,
1589, 1528, 1476, 1418, 1130, 961, 751 cm-1; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd. for
C19H12N2F6 [M+Na]+: 405.0802, found: 405.0814.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM screw-capped vial used
