$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: B. Sodium hydride (60% suspension in oil,
0.120 g, 3.0 mmol) was added to a solution of the aromatic amine (3.0
mmol) in N,N-dimethylaniline (5 ml), and then (after the hydrogen
evolution ceased) 1,3,7-triazapyrene (1) (0.103 g, 0.5 mmol) was added.
The mixture was heated to 80-85°C and stirred at that temperature for the
duration indicated in Table 1. The further isolation was performed
according to the method A. 6-(Pyridin-2-ylamino)-1,3,7-triazapyrene (2c).
Yield 0.120 g (81%), light-brown crystals, time: 8 h. mp 232-233°C
(EtOAc). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 7.17 (1H, dd, J = 7.0, J = 7.3,
H-5 Py); 7.89 (1H, dd, J = 8.3, J = 7.3, H-4 Py); 7.95 (1H, d, J = 9.0,
H-4); 8.18 (1H, d, J = 9.3, H-10); 8.36 (1H, d, J = 8.3, H-3 Py); 8.45
(1H, br. d, J = 7.0, H-6 Py); 8.70 (1H, d, J = 9.0, H-5); 9.34 (1H, d, J
= 9.3, H-9); 9.46 (1H, s, H-8); 9.67 (1H, s, H-2); 10.63 (1H, br. s, NH).
Found, m/z: 298.1088 [M+H]+. C18H12N5. Calculated, m/z: 298.1087.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
