$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure C: Synthesis of indolines
via Pd-catalyzed intramolecular amination of δ -C(sp2)-H bonds (condition
A). A mixture of picolinamide (1.0 mmol, 1.0 eq), Pd(OAc)2 (4.5 mg, 0.02
mmol, 0.02 eq), PhI(OAc)2 (645 mg, 2.0 mmol, 2.0 eq) and toluene (8 mL)
in a 20 mL glass vial (purged with Ar, sealed with PTFE cap) was heated
at 60 °C for 24 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt, and
concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was purified by silica gel
flash chromatography to give the cyclized product. Compound 15 was
prepared following the standard procedure C in 81%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400
MHz) δ 8.51 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 8.41 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 8.10 (d, J =
7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.85 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 7.38-7.36 (m, 1H), 7.30-7.26 (m,
1H), 7.20 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.10 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 5.81 (d, J =
10.2 Hz, 1H), 3.65-3.59 (m, 1H), 3.61 (s, 3H), 3.26 (d, J = 16.2 Hz, 1H);
13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ 172.58, 165.14, 152.68, 146.96, 143.38,
137.12, 129.07, 127.59, 125.35, 124.91, 124.41, 124.24, 117.86, 62.41,
52.23, 33.58; HRMS Calcd for C16H15N2O3 [M+H+]: 283.1077; Found:
283.1061.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, capped vial used, alternative reaction conditions shown,
alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield, major product depends
on reaction temperature
