$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6. One-pot Direct Amination using NCS5 To an amber 8 mL-vial (vial A),
[Cp*RhCl2]2 (2.5 mol %, 3.1 mg), CsOAc (30 mol %, 11.5 mg) and AgSbF6
(1.5 equiv, 103 mg) were added, and the vial was sealed with a Teflon®
liner cap. To another amber 4-mL vial, N-chlorosuccinimide (1.2 equiv,
32.4 mg) was added and was also sealed with a Teflon® liner cap (vial B).
Both vials were evacuated and back filled with N2 for three times.
Freshly distilled THF (0.5 mL) and amine (1.1 equiv) were added to the
vial B, and the mixture was stirred at room temperature for 20 min.
Freshly distilled THF (0.5 mL) was then added to the vial A, followed by
the addition of oxime (0.2 mmol) with a 50-μL syringe. The mixture in
vial A was preheated at 40 °C for 5 min. The mixture in vial B was
transferred to vial A with an 1-mL syringe in one portion. The reaction
mixture was allowed to stir at 40 °C for 1 h. After cooling to room
temperature, 30% aqueous ammonia (2 mL) and EtOAc (5 mL) were added. The
organic layer was collected, and the aqueous layer was washed with EtOAc
(5 mL x 2). The combined organic fractions were dried over Na2SO4 and
then filtered through a short plug of Celite®. Solvents were removed by
rotary evaporation, and the residue was re-dissolved in a small amount of
dichloromethane (DCM) for flash column chromatography. 3aa, yield 80%. Rf
= 0.3 (10% EtOAc in hexanes); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δH 7.35-7.28 (m,
2H), 7.06-7.02 (m, 2H), 3.96 (s, 3H), 3.81 (bt, J = 4.8 Hz, 4H), 2.99
(bt, J = 4.8 Hz, 4H), 2.25 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δC 158.41
(C), 150.45 (C), 132.00 (C), 130.29 (CH), 129.76 (CH), 123.02 (CH),
118.48 (CH), 67.20 (CH2), 61.63 (CH3), 52.21 (CH2), 15.11 (CH3); IR
(neat, cm-1): 2959, 2852, 2817, 1487, 1447, 1225, 1119, 1054, 1039, 881;
HRMS m/z (ESI): calculated for C13H19N2O2+: 235.1447, found: 235.1437.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, alternative preparation shown, amber vial used, the
mixture from the first stage and the mixture from the second stage were
mixed the third stage, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rhodium(III)-Catalyzed Intermolecular Direct Amination of Aromatic C-H
Bonds with N-Chloroamines
