$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for the Preparation of
2-Aminobenzimidazoles 3a-p by the Reaction of Arylguanidine and
Phenyliodine(III) Bis(trifloroacetate): In a 25 mL of flask,
phenyliodine(III) bis(trifloroacetate) (0.33 mmol, 146 mg) was added to
an arylguanidine (0.30 mmol) in MeCN (5 mL), and the mixture was stirred
at 80 °C temperature for 4 h. The solvent of the reaction mixture was
evaporated under vacuum. The residue was purified by chromatography with
PE and ethyl acetate to give products. Compound 3k. Yield: 80% (0.3 mmol,
70 mg), yellow solid. mp: 48.6-49.5 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.92
(t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H, CH3), 1.32-1.41 (m, 2H, CH2), 1.55-1.63 (m, 2H, CH2),
2.34 (s, 3H, CH3), 2.46 (s, 3H, CH3), 3.49 (q, J = 6.7 Hz,, 2H, CH2),
4.11, (brs, 1H, NH), 6.71 (s, 1H, CH), 6.93 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H, CH),
7.26-7.40 (m, 5H, CH); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 13.76, 20.00, 21.16,
21.42, 31.86, 43.01, 108.17, 115.71, 122.53, 126.81, 129.40, 130.94,
132.15, 135.45, 138.75, 140.25, 153.49. HRMS calcd. for C19H 24N3 [M+H]+
: 294.1970, found 294.1965.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Oxidant-Switchable Selective Synthesis of 2-Aminobenzimidazoles via C-H
Amination/Acetoxylation of Guanidines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chi, Yue; Zhang, Wen-Xiong; Xi, Zhenfeng
